<title>USA: Kellogg declines comment on bid rumors.</title>
<headline>Kellogg declines comment on bid rumors.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kellogg Co, the largest cereal maker in the United States, on Wednesday declined to comment on market rumors that Unilever Plc might make a bid for it.</p>
<p>&quot;We can't comment on rumors,&quot; Kellogg spokeman Anthony Hebron said.</p>
<p>According to dealers in Europe, Anglo-Dutch conglomerate Unilever was rumored to be considering a bid for Kellogg's.</p>
<p>Traders said rumors gathered momentum after the European Commission on Tuesday cleared the sale of Unilever's four specialty chemical units to ICI. Speculation was centered around how Unilever might use the $8.0 billion in proceeds from the sale.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
